  "body": "Part 3 of #917. The maintainer's direction on #917: remove `truck-stepio` and `ruststep` fully.\n\n## What is wrong\n\nAfter parts 1 and 2 of #917, no app code reads STEP through `truck-stepio` or `ruststep`. The two crates stay in the workspace:\n\n- the root `Cargo.toml` (the pins, the rationale text, the `[patch.crates-io]` entry for `ruststep`)\n- the dev-dependencies of `crates/kernel` (the comparison bench reads STEP through truck)\n- `Cargo.lock`\n\n## What to do\n\n- Remove the truck side of the kernel comparison bench, or replace it with recorded readings. Record the decision in `docs/decisions/`.\n- Remove the two crates from each `Cargo.toml` and from `Cargo.lock`.\n- Keep `truck` only where code that does not read STEP needs it. Name each such use in the PR body.\n- The `#[test]` count does not go down without a named reason.\n\n## Order\n\nThis issue is stacked on part 2. Its PR completes #917 (`Fixes #917`).\n\nRefs #917\n",
